==English==
{{was wotd|2007|June|19}}

===Etymology===
First attested in 1615. From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|somnolent}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|sompnolent}}, subsequently from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|somnolentus}}, {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|somnus||sleep}}, {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*swépnos}}, {{m|ine-pro|*súpnos||dream}}, which both are derived from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*swep-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈsɒmnələnt/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈsɑːmnələnt/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-somnolent.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[drowsy|Drowsy]] or [[sleepy]].
# {{label|en|dated}} Causing literal or figurative sleepiness; [[soporific]].

